# Terraform standards

Canonical detail: `AGENTS.md`.

- Optional AWS skeleton lives under `infra/terraform/`. Delete it if the project does not need Terraform.
- All infrastructure is code. No console-driven resource changes.
- Never commit secret values or real cloud account IDs. Prefer data sources (for example `data.aws_caller_identity`) and placeholders such as `<ACCOUNT_ID>` or `<STATE_BUCKET>` in examples.
- Keep state and `.tfvars` with real values out of git (see `.gitignore`).
- Before finishing: `terraform fmt -check -recursive`, `terraform init -backend=false`, and `terraform validate`. CI runs those when `infra/**` changes.
- Keep infrastructure PRs intentional and small.
